  ('world-083', 3, 'Add the mushrooms and the tomato cut into wedges and cook for 3 minutes.'),
  ('world-083', 4, 'Add the shrimp and simmer for 2 to 3 minutes, just until they turn pink.'),
  ('world-083', 5, 'Take the pot off the heat and stir in the fish sauce and lime juice. Taste: it should be sour, salty and hot.'),
  ('world-083', 6, 'Scatter with cilantro. The lemongrass and ginger are for flavour and are not eaten.'),
  ('world-085', 1, 'Pound or finely chop the garlic and chilies together.'),
  ('world-085', 2, 'Mix the soy sauce, oyster sauce, fish sauce and sugar with a tablespoon of water.'),
  ('world-085', 3, 'Heat 2 tablespoons of the oil in a wok over high heat and fry the garlic and chilies for 15 seconds.'),
  ('world-085', 4, 'Add the minced chicken, breaking it up, and stir-fry for 3 to 4 minutes until cooked and starting to brown.'),
  ('world-085', 5, 'Pour in the sauce and toss for a minute, then fold in the basil until it wilts.'),
  ('world-085', 6, 'Fry the eggs in the remaining oil until the edges are crisp. Serve the chicken over rice with an egg on top.'),
  ('world-093', 1, 'Rinse the glutinous rice until the water runs clear and soak it for at least 4 hours, or overnight.'),
  ('world-093', 2, 'Drain the rice and steam it in a cloth-lined steamer for 20 to 25 minutes until tender and translucent.'),
  ('world-093', 3, 'Meanwhile, gently warm the coconut milk with the sugar and salt until dissolved. Do not let it boil.'),
  ('world-093', 4, 'Tip the hot rice into a bowl and stir in about three quarters of the coconut milk. Cover and rest for 15 minutes so the rice absorbs it.'),
